WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:50.780
[COLONEL] Oh, bully! And here I thought I was gonna be the last guest to arrive.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:56.240
My friends call me the Colonel. You're welcome to do the same, should it please you. But, uh...

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.580
...after you.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.520
[BUTLER] Ah, bonjour! Welcome to Markiplier Manor. Your invitation, please.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:17.780
Very good, very good. Right this way. Good luck at the table tonight. I shall fetch you a drink forthwith.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.200
[MAYOR] Oh! There you are, old friend. How are you settling into your new office?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.120
Now I know it'll take some getting used to, but there's no one I would rather have alongside me to protect this great city of ours.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.320
Now, I'll see you at the table soon, but try not to rob me blind again. We'll catch up.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.100
[CHEF] If you're looking for hors d'oeuvres, I'll get 'em when I'm good and ready!

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.820
And stay out of my kitchen!

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.220
[BUTLER] Now, now. Let's not be rude to our guest.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.580
So sorry about that.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.780
Here's your champagne.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.200
Enjoy your evening.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.640
[MARK] Welcome, welcome, one and all!

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:13.780
My name is Markiplier. Thank you for joining me on this auspicious evening. So good to be surrounded by such close and trusted friends.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.100
Now, this evening, it's not all about the poker. It's not all about me.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.700
It's about you.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.120
So drink up and be merry! Life is for the living! And who knows?

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.980
I could be dead tomorrow.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:34.820
[laughter, slowly becomes distorted]

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:40.000
[EDM plays through scene]

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.640
[music distorts and fades]

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.300
[clock ticking]

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:07.000
[alarm rings]

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.220
[BUTLER] Ah, good morning. Hope you've had a good night's rest.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:22.680
I've prepared for you a seltzer with cocaine. Best thing for the morning after, if you ask me.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:32.440
[MAYOR] Ah, there's our little monster! You really knocked 'em dead last night. I haven't seen you go wild like that since our days at university.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.080
Good to let the beast out every once in a while, eh, old friend?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.860
Then again, I'm-I'm still not exactly sure as to what we're supposed to be celebrating here.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:46.340
I mean it's good to have the gang back together, but...out of the blue like this seems...

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:52.740
Anyway, now is not the time to become conspiratorial. Life is ours to choose, as I always say.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.440
I have some work to finish, but I'll meet you at breakfast. We'll all catch up soon.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.600
[DETECTIVE] Did anyone hear that lightning?

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.460
OH MY GOD! THERE'S BEEN A MURDER!

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.540
[BUTLER] Excuse me, did you hear light—OH MY GOD MURDER!

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.680
[CHEF] Did you—? MUUUURDER!

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.480
[DETECTIVE] What the hell happened here? Who's in charge around here?

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.480
Trick question: that guy. And he's dead now, which makes ME in charge.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:42.480
So you better listen up good, bucko. 'Case you haven't been paying attention, there's been a bit of a...killin'.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.200
And you're my prime suspect!

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:52.100
So you better get to explaining right quick as to the what, where, when and why you happen to be here upon this man's death!

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:55.680
[BUTLER] Sir, the body is cold. He's been dead a while.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.160
[DETECTIVE] (chuckles) A likely story!

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:03.080
That I happen to believe completely. All right, you're off the hook for now, but I'm a detective, and—

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.020
[CHEF] Oh, yeah? Prove you're a real dick!

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.680
[DETECTIVE] Here's my badge. Asshole.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:14.960
Ah, Those are my old partners. Don't ask me about them. Fine! I'll tell you.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:21.720
Each one of them died. Each death more tragic than the last. A few of them even died in ironically hilarious ways.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.300
Which made it all the more tragic.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:29.140
But hey, you look like you're up to the task. You're my new partner.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:35.740
(laughs) That's what all my old partners used to say. Right before they died.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.160
All right. Hand me that fingerprinting kit behind you, partner.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:45.240
Thanks, partner.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:54.240
[MAYOR] What the hell happened here?

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.100
[BUTLER] Oh! Mr. Mayor. I'm so sorry. There's been a murder.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:58.920
[thunderclap]

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.000
[MAYOR] A murder?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.280
[another thunderclap]

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:01.880
Who?

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.200
[CHEF] It's Mark.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.620
[DETECTIVE] I'm afraid he's telling the truth.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:09.240
Mark's been...killed.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.880
[MAYOR] Why? Who would do this?

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.800
[DETECTIVE] That's exactly what me and my new partner here are here to find out.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:19.580
[BUTLER] Um, excuse me. I feel like we should call the authorities for them to handle this matter.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:23.260
[DETECTIVE] Look, buddy, as far as you're concerned, I AM the authorities.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:28.320
The fact of the matter is, I believe the killer is right here amongst us in this very house.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.700
With that freaky lightning storm outside, none of us would get very far, anyway.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:39.220
So, in the meantime, we're stuck here. But I'm gonna get to the bottom of this.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:44.540
The rest of you, get back to your rooms, hunker down, and pray to God you're not next to be murdered.

00:06:44.549 --> 00:06:45.920
[thunderclap]

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.880
[BUTLER] I'll...I'll check on our other guests.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:52.920
[CHEF] I'll get back to cooking. All this death made me hungry.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.640
[MAYOR] I...I-I need to talk to the Colonel about this.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.620
[DETECTIVE] All right, partner. It's time to get to work.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:08.100
Judging by the temperature of the body that I measured rectally,

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:13.840
which is obviously the most accurate way to get the inner body temperature of a corpse. That's a fact, totally procedure.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:19.520
Don't tell anyone I did it. I am sure Mark was killed around 1:30 a.m. last night.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:23.620
So what were YOU doing at 1:30 a.m. last night?

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:28.300
[EDM music]

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:32.380
[DETECTIVE] I'm gonna ignore the strange fact that you sleep with your eyes open.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:33.940
But it checks out.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:40.460
So, we need to figure out where everyone was and what they were doing around that time or, at the very least, who saw Mark last.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:45.660
You need to get out there. See if you can piece together the story of what happened last night.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.820
I'll stick around with the body and run more...

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.360
...tests. (deep sniff)

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.920
[MAYOR] Oh, How can you be so flippant?

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.660
[COLONEL] Flippant?! I'm taking this matter very seriously.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.260
[MAYOR] Oh, don't give me that horseshit! I know you hated him, but...goddammit, he reached out to you!

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:04.760
[COLONEL] Oh, what do you want from me, then?

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.280
[MAYOR] Wh—I want you to care!

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.340
[COLONEL] Just because I'm not weeping like a child doesn't mean that I don't care.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.040
[MAYOR] I can't believe you.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:17.360
You come find me when you pull your head out of your ass!

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:20.300
Excuse me.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.320
[COLONEL] Damien, I don't—Oh!

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:33.440
Ah! Good to see you again! You were quite the rapscallion at last night's festivities.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:41.180
But you're probably here to help the detective with his "investigation of murder."

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.640
[thunderclap]

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:48.960
Anyway. I'll help you, I'll tell you what happened to our dear friend Mark.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.340
[COLONEL, mockingly] "Oh, look at me! My name is Markiplier now!"

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:58.840
"Forget all my friends or the people that helped me along the way; just look at my money!"

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:05.380
"Oh, I need to pay people to be my friends! Ha ha ha! You like me? Too bad!"

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:14.760
"Oh, glug glug! Oopsie poopsie! I can't hold my booze. Gotta go off to the little boys' room. Who wants to join me?"

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:20.100
"I'm gonna go there upon my stairs. MY house has more than ONE staircase."

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.980
"Oh, look at me and how great I AM!"

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:27.040
"Oh no, I'm falling! Aaah, I'm dead."

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.240
[COLONEL] And that's what happened. Probably, anyway.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:39.180
So, if you need to corroborate this story with anybody else, just be on your way and investigate the entire house.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:42.640
Go now. I'll be here when you're done.

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:50.840
[BUTLER] Come with me. I need to show you something.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:56.240
Now, if you're looking for answers, there's really no mystery at all.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:01.720
There's not a single detail of this house that I'm not privy to,

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:07.240
and not a single guest that I have not personally vetted.

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:17.360
Now I warn you: what you are about to see is not for the faint of heart. A domain of evil this is...

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:19.420
But in we must go.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.140
You first.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:49.200
AVERT YOUR EYES! I'm so sorry you had to see this!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:11:01.300
Master would be so displeased! If only he were still alive! (loud sobbing that gradually fades)

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.480
[CHEF] I thought I told you to stay out of my kitchen!

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:19.600
Oh. You're helping that dick with his little investigation, huh?

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:24.140
Well, I might look like a sweet and innocent man,

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:31.120
but some people with short lifespans might think otherwise. I can't imagine why, can you?

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:36.720
Last night, after I got rid of all of the evidence...

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:42.700
...of that delicious meal I prepared, and wiped down all the fingerprints...

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.440
...from those filthy dishes.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.440
And sopped up all that blood...

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:56.940
I retired to my room at 1:00 a.m. and left my little buddy in charge, like I always do.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:04.700
He sees everything. Why don't you ask HIM what happened last night?

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.300
[MARK] Abe!
[DETECTIVE] Mark! Good to see ya.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:41.780
[MARK] Great to see ya. Look, I'll cut right to the chase. Chef, butler, good?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:48.620
[DETECTIVE] Chef's an asshole, but he's clean. Uh...butler, he's a new guy. Also an asshole, but he's also clean

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.440
[MARK] Well, I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:19.840
[soft piano music, birds chirping]

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:37.020
[MAYOR] (sighs) Look, I'm sorry you saw that argument with the Colonel. I lost my temper, and it wasn't right and...he must be in shock.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:41.620
The Colonel's an eccentric; it's his best quality and his worst.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:47.760
But he's my friend, and...so was Mark.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:52.080
I know I'm supposed to be a leader in this scenario, but I can't help but feel lost!

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:55.040
I've known Mark for years, since we were kids!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:57.620
And he's just gone?

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:07.800
I don't have any answers right now. I just need to be alone...to process all of this.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.980
We'll talk soon, but I need to think.

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:17.460
[DETECTIVE] Hey! Partner! Get over here, now! Hurry up!

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:24.760
You're not gonna believe this; I can barely believe this! The body: it's gone. It's just fucking disappeared. Look!

